From 8e8273c162025eb3f27051e7b69aa6109ebedf35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:09:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Wire the cockpit display module into a FreeRTOS task

Adds cockpit_task.c/.h: brings up both panels via
cockpitDisplayBegin(), shows the boot splash once, then loops
rendering the PFD onto CS1 and the moving map onto CS2.

Started from main.c alongside srxl2_task, at lower priority (1 vs
srxl2_task's 3) so rendering never delays SRXL2 frame handling.

Pitch/roll/heading are a synthetic sweep for now, not read from the
IMU (not ported yet) - this is purely so the panels visibly come
alive once flashed, as a checkpoint before the servo and IMU ports.
Airspeed/altitude/VSI reuse the same fixed demo values the original
Arduino sketch used.

Builds and links cleanly (0 warnings) on top of the previous
display-driver-and-renderer patch.
---
 board/project/cockpit/CMakeLists.txt |  1 +
 board/project/cockpit/cockpit_task.c | 85 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 board/project/cockpit/cockpit_task.h | 10 ++++
 board/project/constants.h            |  2 +
 board/project/main.c                 |  4 ++
 5 files changed, 102 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 board/project/cockpit/cockpit_task.c
 create mode 100644 board/project/cockpit/cockpit_task.h

